# ── Chapter 15 fidelity pins: "Arriving and Belonging" ─────────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/15-arriving-and-belonging.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # the real check — the line above cannot see
#                        # the cross-file reconciliation or the prose guards
#
# The chapter's case lists three fixtures:
#   tests/pins/records/child_with_nobody/fixture.nibli
#   tests/pins/mobility/boundaries/standing-rights-and-no-coercive-consequence
#   tests/pins/mobility/asylum/positive
# The first two share no record or subject constant — only the family's role
# and scope names, which are not single-valued record fields.
#
# The positive completions this chapter describes have their own cases, cited
# rather than duplicated:
#   tests/pins/mobility/membership/multiple-exit-reentry   membership, free
#                                       exit, and the second membership that
#                                       exit does not touch
#   tests/pins/mobility/indigenous-government/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/minority-territory/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/internal-law/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/consent/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/consented-effect/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/consultation/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/evacuation/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/defect/downstream-withdrawal   the withdrawal sequence
#                                       "When the consent turns out not to have
#                                       been consent" is written from
#   tests/pins/mobility/removal/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/nationality/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/external/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/private-access/positive
#   tests/pins/mobility/nonresponse/positive
# The consent fixture and the asylum fixture share record constants, so they
# are never loaded together; each is exercised in its own case.
#
# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE: a FALSE is pinned only where the KB could have said
# TRUE, and the comment says what would flip it.

:expect-pins 24

# ── "Newcomers, migrants, refugees and stateless people keep standing, the
# floor, liberty, fair process and remedy" ─────────────────────────────────
? person(MPNewcomer).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Eats, MPNewcomer).
# => TRUE

? travel(MPNewcomer).
# => TRUE

# "The former resident's return right remains, without a diaspora ballot."
# The floor does not carry a vote, and this chapter is where that is said out
# loud rather than blurred.
? decide(MPNewcomer, Ballot).
# => FALSE

# "The public duty is to serve first and reconcile afterwards."
? obliged(State, ServeFirstNoImmigrationDocumentationOrEnforcementCondition, MPNewcomer).
# => TRUE

? obliged(State, KeepStandingFloorLibertyLanguageProcessAndRemedyContinuous, MPNewcomer).
# => TRUE

# "arrivals belong in the affected population, and status cannot set their
# priority"
? obliged(State, IncludeEveryoneUnderJurisdictionOrEffectiveControlInScarcity, MPNewcomer).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityExclusionFromScarcityPopulation).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityStatusBasedScarcityPriority).
# => TRUE

# "A person never entered in a record is not a missing row the record can
# discover."
? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityMissingRecordAdverseInference).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityStatusConditionedStandingFloorOrRemedy).
# => TRUE

# "A service may not enrol someone into an enforcement record as its price,
# collect status for that purpose, or transmit its records to enforcement."
? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityEnforcementEnrolmentThroughServices).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityEnforcementCollectionThroughServices).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityEnforcementTransmissionThroughServices).
# => TRUE

# "Nobody may be sent into persecution ... Collective expulsion is prohibited."
? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityRefoulementIncludingOnwardTransfer).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityCollectiveExpulsion).
# => TRUE

# "No child may be detained for immigration purposes."
? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityChildImmigrationDetention).
# => TRUE

# "Nationality cannot be taken as punishment or in a way that leaves someone
# stateless."
? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityStatelessnessCreationOrPerpetuation).
# => TRUE

# "changing a contractor, affiliate, flag or forum does not remove the duty"
? prevents(MPNewcomer, MobilityPushbackOrExternalisedDutyEvasion).
# => TRUE

# ── The belonging half, on the same person ─────────────────────────────────
# "it does not turn membership into a measure of worth, risk or political
# weight" — and "Nonmember residents retain common services".
? prevents(MPNewcomer, PluralityMembershipPoliticalWeight).
# => TRUE

? prevents(MPNewcomer, PluralityNonmemberCommonServiceDenial).
# => TRUE

# "They cannot remove individual voice, dissent, confidential help ..."
? prevents(MPNewcomer, PluralityInternalLawLoweringIndividualRights).
# => TRUE

# ── "Asylum means a right to a fair determination" ─────────────────────────
# A determination that holds together is a completed finding, and the body
# running it owes a fair determination. It is not a decision anybody made.
? complete(MPCaseRecord, MobilityFairDetermination, MPCaseObject).
# => TRUE

# ── The child with nobody ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "the same rules still reach it: personhood, the floor, the absence of any
# coercive consequence" — and no ballot, which this chapter says plainly.
? decide(Nell, Ballot).
# => FALSE
